<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1810–1859</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as King Bomba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> from 1830 to 1859. He opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s first railway, from Naples to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portici">Portici</a>, in 1839. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Palermo</a> rising of January 1848 against him began the revolutions of that year; he granted and then withdrew a constitution and reconquered Sicily by bombarding its cities, earning the nickname King Bomba.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-ii-of-the-two-sicilies.jpg" alt="Ferdinand II of the Two Sicilies" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alphonse Bernoud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferdinand_II_of_the_Two_Sicilies_1859.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
